          "title": "Narendra Karmarkar",
          "meta": "IIT Bombay, B.Tech. EE 1978",
          "body": "Developed Karmarkar's algorithm at Bell Labs in 1984 — a breakthrough polynomial-time interior-point method for linear programming. Fulkerson Prize recipient; his work transformed global logistics, telecommunications and finance.",
          "link": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narendra_Karmarkar"
        },
        {
          "title": "Arun Netravali",
          "meta": "IIT Bombay, B.Tech. EE 1967",
          "body": "MS and PhD at Rice; joined Bell Labs in 1972 and became its ninth President. Pioneered the video compression standards that became the foundation of MPEG — digital TV, HDTV and streaming video. Also worked at NASA (1970–72) on space shuttle problems.",
          "link": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arun_Netravali"
        },
        {
          "title": "Vinod Khosla",
          "meta": "IIT Delhi, B.Tech. EE 1976",
          "body": "Co-founded Sun Microsystems in 1982 at 27 as founding CEO, pioneering open systems, commercial RISC processors and Java. Founded Khosla Ventures in 2004, managing roughly $16 billion. Early OpenAI investor.",
          "link": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vinod_Khosla"
        }
